      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Perrysburg%2C_Ohio"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Fort Meigs, built in 1815 on the Maumee River, honors Ohio governor Return Jonathan Meigs and stands as a Civil War landmark.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6,
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Perrysburg%2C_Ohio"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Dayton and Michigan Railroad reached Perrysburg in 1859, later becoming part of the Baltimore and Ohio network.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Perrysburg%2C_Ohio"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A 19th‑century hydraulic canal diverted river water to power grist, saw, tannery, furniture, paper, and machine shops along the waterfront.",
